// A height chart's pixel's edge, from its own surface (docs/frame.md, "The edge record"): its
// outline, where the surface turns from the eye (a wave's crest against the sky, a dune's brow
// against the sea beyond it, the far edge of the ground at the horizon), is where n·v falls to
// nothing; so it is n·v over how fast n·v falls across the pixel away, the way it falls fastest.
// No search of the screen.
//
// The way to it is lib/frame's (`frame::outline::way_to_outline`), as every lister's is.

/// How strong the line is where a height chart meets the sky far off (its horizon): the old
/// ink's horizon was a thin line of 0.18 (rywible/wrela 7ae6711e, content/humanoid/ink.wrela:295,
/// against the backdrop), which the frame's outline weight (0.75) gives from 0.24.
pub const HORIZON: f32 = 0.24
